        "message": "Evaluate the Wait hold on the native-ingest path with settling-tail proof\n\nThe second GPU-rendering trial eliminated every physics stall and passed\nall checks except the wait-interval zero contract: the earlier hold-timing\nfix let the hold fire while the native still applied the -0.010\ndeceleration step, so the measured interval began one pre-zero sample\nearly. The hold now again requires the native applied value inside the\n<=0.005 settling tail that the wait-metrics contract itself permits, and\nthe adapter exposes maybe_wait_hold() evaluated on the pump's\nnative-ingest path (~650 Hz) so renewal fires within milliseconds of the\nnative confirming the tail instead of racing the command deadline on the\nslower observer pass that lost the first pilot by 0.2 ms. This closes\nboth races: the deadline race via fast evaluation, the interval-start\nrace via native confirmation. Regression tests updated to the corrected\ncontract; 170 safety tests pass. The second GPU trial's evidence is\nretained."
      },
